        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "A roster battle that had been simmering all camp finally snapped into focus - and the Leafs did the sensible thing. <strong>Toronto signed Nick Blankenburg to a one-year deal</strong>, turning a PTO into a real job after he flashed enough bite and mobility to stick. That's the kind of depth move contenders make, not afterthought clubs. The club is still officially 0-0-0 and first in the Atlantic with zero points, but that clean slate disappears Tuesday night in Montreal. The bigger picture is straightforward: the Leafs' new-look blue line needs players who can survive the grind, not merely survive camp. Blankenburg's arrival, and the hard cut decisions that followed, say this group is trimming fat fast. <strong>Now comes the real test - the opener in Montreal, and the first answer on whether this rebuilt roster can play with some edge.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 28, 2026"
      },
