      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The season didn't merely end; it slid out with a familiar thud, leaving Toronto with hard questions and a thin layer of consolation after <strong>a 5-1 win over the Reds in the finale</strong>. At 79-83 and fifth in the AL East, this club finished as a subtraction problem - too little power, too many empty nights, too many veterans headed for free agency. Max Scherzer's seven scoreless-looking innings? Not enough to change the ledger. George Springer and Kevin Gausman may be gone, the coaching staff may not be, and John Schneider's club now has to decide whether to reload around Vladimir Guerrero Jr. or retool more ruthlessly. <strong>What matters next is the roster churn - who stays, who walks, and whether Toronto finally commits to a cleaner, younger core.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 28, 2026"
      },
