        "body": "A team can breathe again after a win like that - but only just. <strong>Washington's 33-31 stunner over Seattle</strong> was the kind of October-survival football that buys a locker room time and a little swagger, with Marcus Mariota throwing three touchdowns and the defense cashing in on turnovers when it had to. At 1-2, third in the NFC East and 1.5 games back, the Commanders still have work to do, but the first pulse is there. The uglier news came with Leo Chenal's season-ending neck surgery, a gut punch in the middle of the defense, even as Austin Ekeler's expected return adds needed juice to a thin backfield. Mariota has steadied the ship. <strong>Next comes Indianapolis on Oct. 4 - and Washington needs this win to prove Sunday was more than a jolt.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 28, 2026"
      },
