  "morning_brief": {
    "article": {
      "title": "Mariota Lifts Commanders Past Seahawks",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Marcus Mariota threw three touchdown passes and the Commanders held on for a 33-31 win over the Seahawks last night, a tidy road-type result that gives Washington something real to build on this week. The next test comes Sunday morning against the Colts, with kickoff set for 9:30 AM ET on NFL Net.",
        "For Toronto, Max Scherzer closed the Blue Jays season with seven-plus innings and seven strikeouts in a 5-1 win over the Reds, while Charles McAdoo added a homer. The Maple Leafs have signed defenceman Nick Blankenburg to a one-year contract and open the season Tuesday night against the Canadiens on Sportsnet, and the Raptors are in camp with preseason action against the Heat on Oct. 3 before the regular season opens against the Bulls on Oct. 21."
      ]
    }
  }
